23,draft_0299,train,Cloud Security,NIST.SP.800-215.txt,What technique is used to prevent lateral movement in reducing the attack surface?,Techniques like microsegmentation are used to prevent lateral movement in reducing the attack surface.,"Guide to a Secure Enterprise • The access level determined by the previous process is continuously reevaluated during the user session and recalibrated if required. As the context surrounding the identity changes in real time, so can the user’s entitlements [31]. • The attack surface is reduced by preventing lateral movement [32] through techniques like microsegmentation, as described in Section 5.1. With the increasing deployment of microservices, the inter-services resource requests (generator of east-west traffic) dominate external application requests (north-south traffic). Application of this principle thus secures east-west traffic. In all security frameworks for current enterprise network environments, the common principles that underlie application-specific requirements – such as low latency, high data transfer rates, and high reliability – that were applicable in previous network landscapes remain the same. Guide to a Secure Enterprise Secure Wide Area Network Infrastructure for an Enterprise Network The wide area network (WAN) became an integral part of the enterprise network when organizations needed to connect their local area networks (LANs) across multiple geographically distributed locations (within the country and, in some cases, globally) starting in the 1980s. The initial WAN technology involved point-to-point (P2P) leased lines followed by frame relay. The first IP-based network was multiprotocol label switching (MPLS), which enabled multiple types of traffic – such as voice, video, and data – to travel on the same line. With the advent of technologies such as virtualization and increasing enterprise access to cloud services, enterprises have begun to adopt a new WAN technology called the software-defined wide area network (SD-WAN). SD-WAN technology removes the tight coupling between the control plane and data plane functions of the network and enables the centralized specification of various policies, such as access control, routing, and applica",,,,,ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.78,"user’s entitlements [31]. • The attack surface is reduced by preventing lateral movement [32] through techniques like microsegmentation, as described in Section 5.1. With the increasing deployment of microservices, the inter-services resource requests (generator of east-west traffic) dominate external application requests (north-south traffic). Application of this principle thus secures east-west traffic. In all security frameworks for current enterprise network environments, the common principles that underlie application-specific requirements",ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.78,"user’s entitlements [31]. • The attack surface is reduced by preventing lateral movement [32] through techniques like microsegmentation, as described in Section 5.1. With the increasing deployment of microservices, the inter-services resource requests (generator of east-west traffic) dominate external application requests (north-south traffic). Application of this principle thus secures east-west traffic. In all security frameworks for current enterprise network environments, the common principles that underlie application-specific requirements"
24,kaggle1000_0867,train,Cloud Security,Cyber.Security_.Analytics.Technology.and.Automation.txt,What types of systems are considered critical infrastructure in Australia according to the Australian Government's definition?,"According to the Australian Government's definition, critical infrastructure in Australia includes physical facilities, supply chains, information technologies, and communication networks that, if destroyed, degraded, or rendered unavailable for an extended period, would significantly impact the social or economic wellbeing of the nation or affect Australia's ability to conduct national defense and ensure national security. Specifically, Trusted Information Sharing Network (TISN) 2007 mentions that Information and Communications Technology (ICT) systems, including Industrial Control Systems (ICS) and Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) systems, form a key part of Australia's critical infrastructure.","The example also demonstrates that attacks can occur internally within an organisation; attacks do not always have to come from external sources. 4 Australian Strategic Cyber Protection Australia’s state and territory governments have deﬁned critical infrastructure as those physical facilities, supply chains, information technologies and communication networks which, if destroyed, degraded or rendered unavailable for an extended period, would signiﬁcantly impact on the social or economic wellbeing of the nation or affect Australia’s ability to conduct national defence and ensure national security (Australian Government ICS and SCADA systems form a key part of Australia’s critical infrastructure. They are used to remotely monitor and control the delivery of essential services and products, such as electricity, gas, water, waste treatment and transport systems (Trusted Information Sharing Network (TISN) 2007). The initial focus of the Australian Federal Government critical infrastructure protection policy (including ICS/SCADA systems) was that critical infrastructure protection was a commercial consideration and related only to information security (Busuttil and Warren 2004). The Australian Federal Government had been aware of the problems that Australian corporations may have in dealing with these security issues and responded by offering advice for corporations. The initial Australian Government advice, in (1998), suggested ways in which organisations could reduce critical infrastructure risks in the following ways (Busuttil and Warren 2004): • Organisations should implement protective security controls such as passwords, etc., in accordance to a deﬁned security standard such as AS/NZS 4444 (now has been replaced with ISO/IEC 27002); • Organisations should formally accredit themselves against information security • Organisations should raise awareness of security issues such as password security, awareness of online risks among their staff; • Organisations should tr",,,,,YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,"Kritik altyapı tanımı, bulut güvenliği özel konusu değil.",System Security,0.78,"physical facilities, supply chains, information technologies and communication networks which, if destroyed, degraded or rendered unavailable for an extended period, would signiﬁcantly impact on the social or economic wellbeing of the nation or affect Australia’s ability to conduct national defence and ensure national security (Australian Government ICS and SCADA systems form a key part of Australia’s critical infrastructure. They are used to remotely monitor and control the delivery of essential services and products, such as electricity, gas,",YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,"Kritik altyapı tanımı, bulut güvenliği özel konusu değil.",System Security,0.78,"physical facilities, supply chains, information technologies and communication networks which, if destroyed, degraded or rendered unavailable for an extended period, would signiﬁcantly impact on the social or economic wellbeing of the nation or affect Australia’s ability to conduct national defence and ensure national security (Australian Government ICS and SCADA systems form a key part of Australia’s critical infrastructure. They are used to remotely monitor and control the delivery of essential services and products, such as electricity, gas,"
25,batch500_0134,train,Cloud Security,Case Studies in Cyber Supply Chain Risk Management_ Anonymous Renewable Energy Company.txt,What specific actions does the Renewable Energy Company take to ensure compliance with regional regulations across its supply chain?,"The Renewable Energy Company is working to merge unique regional regulations into a unified minimum standard across all suppliers. This unified standard aims to simplify compliance and supplier management, ensuring the global cybersecurity posture of the company and its suppliers exceeds any individual region's requirements.","The Renewable Energy Company isolates new plants with an additional access control layer while it identifies and mitigates risks posed by the new assets. The acquired network is monitored and studied by the Case Studies in Cyber Supply Chain Risk Management Anonymous Renewable Energy Renewable Energy Company’s Security Operations Team, and over time, a dedicated team replaces the existing systems at the acquired plant with controlled, mature systems that can be safely integrated with the company’s infrastructure. Every region of the power grid is controlled and coordinated by separate regional transmission organizations (RTO), independent system operators (ISO), and other global equivalents. Each region’s RTO or ISO may establish regulations unique to their region. Power providers, such as the Renewable Energy Company, are responsible for making sure their entire supply chain is compliant with the requirements in a particular region. The company is working to merge these requirements into a unified minimum standard across all suppliers regardless of region. This robust standard would simplify compliance and supplier management while enabling the global cybersecurity posture of the Renewable Energy Company and its suppliers to exceed any one Because power systems are a vital part of critical infrastructure, product reliability and integrity are paramount. The Renewable Energy Company must test for flawed or deliberately compromised hardware and software as well as traditional supply chain risk management functions involved in logistics, materials, and assembly. The company is investing in more thorough and advanced component integrity inspections to mitigate potential supply chain attacks by advanced threat groups. Recognizing the operational and compliance complexity of critical infrastructure logistics, the Renewable Energy Company outsources transit logistics to specialized providers. Recycling is a valuable piece of the Renewable Energy Company’s manufacturing bu",,,,,ALAN_DISI,YUKSEK,Bölgesel mevzuat ve tedarik zinciri uyumu; kullanıcının teknik siber güvenlik kapsamı önceliğinin dışında.,,0.85,"grid is controlled and coordinated by separate regional transmission organizations (RTO), independent system operators (ISO), and other global equivalents. Each region’s RTO or ISO may establish regulations unique to their region. Power providers, such as the Renewable Energy Company, are responsible for making sure their entire supply chain is compliant with the requirements in a particular region. The company is working to merge these requirements into a unified minimum standard across all suppliers regardless of region. This robust standard ",ALAN_DISI,YUKSEK,Bölgesel mevzuat ve tedarik zinciri uyumu; kullanıcının teknik siber güvenlik kapsamı önceliğinin dışında.,,0.85,"grid is controlled and coordinated by separate regional transmission organizations (RTO), independent system operators (ISO), and other global equivalents. Each region’s RTO or ISO may establish regulations unique to their region. Power providers, such as the Renewable Energy Company, are responsible for making sure their entire supply chain is compliant with the requirements in a particular region. The company is working to merge these requirements into a unified minimum standard across all suppliers regardless of region. This robust standard "
26,batch500_0278,val,Cloud Security,Deep Learning Based Behavioral Drift Modeling for Continuous.txt,What is the approximate number of parameters in the lightweight adapter modules used in the Frozen Backbone strategy?,The lightweight adapter modules used in the Frozen Backbone strategy have approximately 512 parameters.,"Environmental Sustainability (Green AI) A critical innovation of this research is its focus on computational efficiency. Traditional adaptive systems require frequent, energy-intensive retraining of deep neural networks to address drift. In contrast, this framework employs a Frozen Backbone strategy. Once the core TCN is trained, only lightweight adapter modules (approx. 512 parameters) are updated. This drastically reduces Floating Point Operations (FLOPs) and carbon footprint over the system lifecycle, making it suitable for resource-constrained edge deployment. D. Project Management and Economic Feasibility The system design was driven by stakeholder feedback emphasizing the need for non-intrusive security that accommodates natural behavioral evolution. • Iterative Design: The project methodology was agile. Initial experiments with Transformers revealed high computational costs and instability, prompting a strategic pivot to the TCN architecture, which offered superior training stability and linear O(n) complexity. • Risk Management: Primary risks included Catastrophic Forgetting (mitigated by freezing the backbone) and Overfitting due to data sparsity (mitigated by sessionrelative normalization and dropout). • Economic Viability: The solution is cost-effective. By eliminating the need for specialized biometric hardware (sensors) and reducing administrative costs associated with false rejections and account recovery, the system offers high economic value. The use of open-source stacks (PyTorch, Ray Tune) kept development costs minimal. This chapter delineates the methodological framework for the proposed Two-Level Behavioral Authentication System. The design is bifurcated into two distinct pipelines: Level 1 addresses fixed-text login verification using the Evo-BioTCN architecture, while Level 2 handles continuous free-text monitoring using a 4-Model Deep Learning Ensemble. A. Level 1: Fixed-Text Methodology (Evo-BioTCN) motivating the fixed-text design is behavi",,,,,ALAN_DISI,YUKSEK,"Frozen Backbone adaptör parametre sayısı, bulut güvenliği değil makine öğrenmesi model mimarisi ayrıntısı.",,0.88,"Traditional adaptive systems require frequent, energy-intensive retraining of deep neural networks to address drift. In contrast, this framework employs a Frozen Backbone strategy. Once the core TCN is trained, only lightweight adapter modules (approx. 512 parameters) are updated. This drastically reduces Floating Point Operations (FLOPs) and carbon footprint over the system lifecycle, making it suitable for resource-constrained edge deployment. D. Project Management and Economic Feasibility The system design was driven by stakeholder feedback ",ALAN_DISI,YUKSEK,"Frozen Backbone adaptör parametre sayısı, bulut güvenliği değil makine öğrenmesi model mimarisi ayrıntısı.",,0.88,"Traditional adaptive systems require frequent, energy-intensive retraining of deep neural networks to address drift. In contrast, this framework employs a Frozen Backbone strategy. Once the core TCN is trained, only lightweight adapter modules (approx. 512 parameters) are updated. This drastically reduces Floating Point Operations (FLOPs) and carbon footprint over the system lifecycle, making it suitable for resource-constrained edge deployment. D. Project Management and Economic Feasibility The system design was driven by stakeholder feedback "
27,extra_20261108_2651,val,Cloud Security,Hacking APIs - Early Access.txt,What are the differences in how cloud providers handle penetration testing requests?,"- **AWS**: Requires permission to conduct testing and includes details such as testing dates, accounts and assets involved, phone number, and a description of the proposed attack.
- **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**: Does not require permission but must comply with the acceptable use policy (AUP) and terms of service (TOS).
- **Microsoft Azure**: Does not require notification and provides a ""Penetration Testing Rules of Engagement"" page.
- **DoS Attacks**: Generally not allowed, but the scope can vary based on the client's risk appetite. Organizations with a high appetite for risk may accept DoS testing, while those with a low appetite may not.","For any exceptions to this, you must email AWS and request permission to conduct testing. If you are requesting an exception, make sure to include your testing dates, any accounts and assets involved, your phone number, and a description of your proposed attack. Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Google simply states that you do not need to request permission or notify the company to perform penetration testing. However, Google also states that you must remain compliant with its acceptable use policy (AUP) and terms of service (TOS) and stay within your authorized scope. The AUP and TOS prohibit illegal actions, phishing, spam, distributing malicious or destructive files (such as viruses, worms, and Trojan horses), and interruption to GCP Microsoft Azure Microsoft takes the hacker-friendly approach and does not require you to notify the company before testing. In addition, it has a “Penetration Testing Rules of Engagement” page that spells .microsoft.com/en-us/msrc/pentest-rules-of-engagement). At least for now, cloud providers are taking a favorable stance toward penetration testing activities. As long as you stay up-to-date with the provider’s terms, you should be operating legally if you only test targets you are authorized to hack and avoid attacks that could cause an interruption to I mentioned that DoS attacks are often off the table. Work with the client to understand their risk appetite for the given engagement. If the customer is Hacking APIs (Early Access) © 2022 by Corey Ball Preparing for API Security TesTing 11 confident about the strength of their infrastructure and is willing to accept the risks associated with DoS attacks. Otherwise, work with the customer to see what they’re willing to allow. DoS attacks represent a huge threat against the security of APIs. An intentional or accidental DoS attack will disrupt the services provided by the target organization, making the API or web application inaccessible. An unplanned business interruption like this is usually a triggering factor for an organization to pursue legal recourse. Therefore, be careful to perform only the testing that you are authorized to perform! Ultimately, whether a client accepts DoS testing as part of the scope depends on the organization’s risk appetite, or the amount of risk an organization is willing to take on to achieve its purpose. Understanding an organization’s risk appetite can help you tailor your testing. If an organization is cutting-edge and has a lot of confidence in its security, it may have a big appetite for risk. An engagement tailored to a large appetite for risk would involve connecting to every feature and running all the exploits you want. On the opposite side of the spectrum are the very risk-averse organizations. Engagements for these organizations will be like walking on eggshells.",,,,,GUNCELLIK_KONTROL,ORTA,AWS izni ifadesi pasajda yalnızca istisnalar için geçiyor; yanıtta genel zorunluluk gibi sunulmuş. Üstelik 2022 politikaları güncel kabul edilemez.,,0.75,"For any exceptions to this, you must email AWS and request permission to conduct testing. If you are requesting an exception, make sure to include your testing dates, any accounts and assets involved, your phone number, and a description of your proposed attack. Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Google simply states that you do not need to request permission or notify the company to perform penetration testing. However, Google also states that you must remain compliant with its acceptable use policy (AUP) and terms of service (TOS) and",GUNCELLIK_KONTROL,ORTA,AWS izni ifadesi pasajda yalnızca istisnalar için geçiyor; yanıtta genel zorunluluk gibi sunulmuş. Üstelik 2022 politikaları güncel kabul edilemez.,,0.75,"For any exceptions to this, you must email AWS and request permission to conduct testing. If you are requesting an exception, make sure to include your testing dates, any accounts and assets involved, your phone number, and a description of your proposed attack. Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Google simply states that you do not need to request permission or notify the company to perform penetration testing. However, Google also states that you must remain compliant with its acceptable use policy (AUP) and terms of service (TOS) and"
28,extra_20261108_4024,val,Cloud Security,Enhanced Security Requirements for Protecting Controlled Unclassified Information_ A Supplement to NIST Special Publication 800-171.txt,What is the purpose of implementing diverse system components in an organizational system according to the relevant security controls?,"The purpose of implementing diverse system components in an organizational system is to reduce the extent of malicious code propagation. This is detailed in control 3.13.1e under ""Create diversity in [Assignment: organization-defined system components] to reduce the extent of malicious code propagation.""","Dynamic Threat Awareness _________________________________________________________________________________________________ Relevant Security Controls 3.11.6e Assess, respond to, and monitor supply chain risks organizational systems and Supply Chain Risk Assessment 3.11.7e Develop a plan for managing supply chain risks associated with organizational systems and system components; update the plan [Assignment: organization-defined _________________________________________________________________________________________________ Relevant Security Controls 3.12.1e Conduct penetration testing [Assignment: organizationdefined frequency], leveraging automated scanning tools and ad hoc tests using subject Supplier Assessments and Testing and Analysis _________________________________________________________________________________________________ Relevant Security Controls 3.13.1e Create diversity in [Assignment: organizationdefined system components] to reduce the extent of malicious code propagation. Security and Privacy Developer Security and Privacy Architecture and Design Platform-Independent Virtualization Techniques Alternate Communications 3.13.2e Implement the following changes to organizational components to introduce a degree of unpredictability into operations: [Assignment: organization-defined changes and frequency of changes by Concealment and Misdirection 3.13.3e Employ [Assignment: organization-defined technical and procedural means] to Transmission Confidentiality Conceal or Randomize Concealment and Misdirection Concealment and Misdirection 3.13.4e Employ [Selection: (one or organization-defined physical isolation techniques]; [Assignment: organizationdefined logical isolation techniques]] in organizational Isolation of Security Tools, Mechanisms, and Support Isolation of System Components Separate Subnets for Connecting to Different Security Domains _________________________________________________________________________________________________ Relevant Security Controls 3.13.5e Distribute and relocate the following system functions or resources [Assignment: organization-defined frequency]: [Assignment: organization-defined system functions or resources]. Concealment and Misdirection Change Processing and Storage _________________________________________________________________________________________________ Relevant Security Controls 3.14.1e Verify the integrity of [Assignment: organizationdefined security critical or essential software] using root of trust mechanisms or cryptographic signatures. Software, Firmware, and Information Integrity Cryptographic Protection Software, Firmware, and Information Integrity Software, Firmware, and Information Integrity Protection of Boot Firmware 3.14.2e Monitor organizational components on an ongoing basis for anomalous or suspicious behavior.",,,,,YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,Kontrol 3.13.1e ile sistem bileşeni çeşitliliği.,System Security,0.71,ad hoc tests using subject Supplier Assessments and Testing and Analysis _________________________________________________________________________________________________ Relevant Security Controls 3.13.1e Create diversity in [Assignment: organizationdefined system components] to reduce the extent of malicious code propagation. Security and Privacy Developer Security and Privacy Architecture and Design Platform-Independent Virtualizati