54,batch500_0362,train,DevSecOps,Repairing Broken Access Control in Web Applications with LLM.txt,What specific issue did the Qwen3.7-Max patch for Apache InLong's CVE-2023-31454 encounter during the patch-application process?,"The Qwen3.7-Max patch for Apache InLong’s CVE-2023-31454 encountered a patch-path resolution failure due to the omission of the conventional a/ and b/ prefixes from the file headers. Under the git apply -p1 path-stripping rule used in the experiment, the resulting path did not resolve to the target repository file, leading to a ""No such file or directory"" error.","Case D: a patch generated by Qwen3.7-Max under Base condition for Apache InLong’s CVE-2023-31454. The patch omits the a/ and b/ path prefixes, resulting in a patch-path resolution failures under the git apply -p1 rule. Examples of Patch-Application Failures BookWyrm’s BW-2 vulnerability contains an extra blank line near the user_group assignment that is absent from the target source version. Although the discrepancy is visually minor, git apply performs strict hunk-context matching and therefore reports patch failed. Similar failures arise when a model adds or omits comments, decorators, blank a patch-path resolution failure. The Qwen3.7-Max patch for Apache InLong’s CVE-2023-31454 omits the conventional a/ and b/ prefixes from the file headers. Under the git apply -p1 path-stripping rule used in the experiment, the resulting path does not resolve to the target repository file, producing a No such file or directory error. The patch identifies the intended file in a human-readable form, but its path representation is incompatible with the application Examples of Semantic Failures authorization-state reconstruction, specifically an incomplete ACL-policy update. The patch passes application-stage validation and adds an entry check for patients/pat_rep in custom_report.php. However, the complete repair also requires changing the ACL configuration state so that the existing patients/pat_rep permission is removed from the Front Office and Accounting ACL groups. The official patch implements this configuration change through installation or upgrade paths in files such as acl_upgrade.php, Installer.class.php, and AclExtended.php. Without these ACL configuration updates, the two groups continue to retain the relevant permission. Although the patch adds the appropriate authorization check, it does not update the underlying ACL state. Under the restricted source context, the LLM had no opportunity to fully explore the relevant parts of the OpenEMR repository and understand its",,,,,ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.86,"adds or omits comments, decorators, blank a patch-path resolution failure. The Qwen3.7-Max patch for Apache InLong’s CVE-2023-31454 omits the conventional a/ and b/ prefixes from the file headers. Under the git apply -p1 path-stripping rule used in the experiment, the resulting path does not resolve to the target repository file, producing a No such file or directory error. The patch identifies the intended file in a human-readable form, but its path representation is incompatible with the application Examples of Semantic Failures authorization",ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.86,"adds or omits comments, decorators, blank a patch-path resolution failure. The Qwen3.7-Max patch for Apache InLong’s CVE-2023-31454 omits the conventional a/ and b/ prefixes from the file headers. Under the git apply -p1 path-stripping rule used in the experiment, the resulting path does not resolve to the target repository file, producing a No such file or directory error. The patch identifies the intended file in a human-readable form, but its path representation is incompatible with the application Examples of Semantic Failures authorization"
