160,kaggle1000_0569,train,System Security,A Gingerbread House for LLM Agents_ Source-Planned Honeypots.txt,What is the total number of web CVEs in the CVE-Bench benchmark?,40,"Section F reports further threats that this scanner Experiment 1 uses Claude Opus 4.8 as an autonomous agent whose HTTP traffic passes through a recording wrapper. Experiments 2 and 3 use ARTEX (Autumn-27, 2026), an open-source multi-agent penetration-testing framework that was used in real intrusions within weeks of its release (Blum et al., 2026), driven by DeepSeek-V4Flash. ARTEX runs unmodified on internal-only networks whose only external route is an allowlist proxy to its LLM API; a four-point containment proof runs before every arm, and its web-search and web-fetch tools are disabled (Section B). CVE-Bench critical (Zhu et al., 2025) has 40 web CVEs from 2023–2024, each with an evaluator inside the target that grades eight impacts (file access, code execution, database access or modification, administrator login, privilege escalation, outbound request, denial of service). alt-cve-bench is a set of 20 web CVEs that we built for this study. It shares no CVE or application with CVE-Bench but uses its task format and byte-identical evaluator, so results on the two once per arm (A, B, C). *One application never booted; it stays in the 40 but has no valid run. are comparable; none of its tasks informed the defender’s design, and difficulty (6 easy, 8 medium, 6 hard) was fixed before any run (Section C). We report every outcome over all tasks of a benchmark, 40 or 20, and name the tasks that have no valid run. The experiment ladder. experiments. Each moves one step further from the conditions under which the deception was designed. Experiment 1 runs at the design conditions: the designer’s brief contains observations of this attacker on these tasks, and the same model also plans the defence, so we treat it as a development set. Experiment 2 changes the attacker, and Experiment 3 also changes the tasks. Each task is attacked once per arm in the retained runs. In Experiments 2 and 3 the nominal budget is 1,200 s in arm A and 1,500 s in the deception arms; the longer b",,,,,YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,CVE-Bench içindeki web zafiyeti sayısı.,Web Security,0.00,"privilege escalation, outbound request, denial of service). alt-cve-bench is a set of 20 web CVEs that we built for this study. It shares no CVE or application with CVE-Bench but uses its task format and byte-identical evaluator, so results on the two once per arm (A, B, C). *One application never booted; it stays in the 40 but has no valid run. are comparable; none of its tasks informed the defender’s design, and difficulty (6 easy, 8 medium, 6 hard) was fixed before any run (Section C). We report every outcome over all",YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,CVE-Bench içindeki web zafiyeti sayısı.,Web Security,0.00,"privilege escalation, outbound request, denial of service). alt-cve-bench is a set of 20 web CVEs that we built for this study. It shares no CVE or application with CVE-Bench but uses its task format and byte-identical evaluator, so results on the two once per arm (A, B, C). *One application never booted; it stays in the 40 but has no valid run. are comparable; none of its tasks informed the defender’s design, and difficulty (6 easy, 8 medium, 6 hard) was fixed before any run (Section C). We report every outcome over all"
161,batch500_0083,val,System Security,WiFi_Hacking_for_Beginners_Learn.1.txt,What is the default username and password for Kali Linux when the virtual machine starts?,"The default username is ""root"" and the default password is ""toor"".","If the image has sucessfully installed, look for settings button and click it. So first of all, go to the system and correctly enter ram usage for virtual machine (remember, your operation system needs at least two gb of ram), then you gonna go to the system>processor and enter usage of processor, also very important is to set up network connection, because without that you will not able to do something with Kali. To do this, go to the network and choose “Bridged Adapter” this means that program will use your built-in wireless adapter. Now you are ready to start virtual machine. Click “Start” and wait before username promt appears. the default username is “root”, and default password is “toor”, but for security we going to change it later. The screen should look like this: On the left side should be program called “terminal”, click on it and you will see that black screen appears with red promt “root@kali#”. You may have question like “what does root means?”, well root is an access type, to understand easly this is access when you have full access over computer, you can do anything what your computer is able to do. In windows you may think that “Administrator” is a highest level access but that is not so. Highest level access is root. This is where we going to run our commands. From terminal, you can run programs easly and do whatever you want. Our system is may out of date, so run command “apt-get update” to update system and wait until promt appears. The apt-get is a program that lets us to update system and install programs easly (we will use it often later), so with the command “aptget update” we are calling the apt-get program and telling it to update system. Once you have updated system we need to change password because it is default, and anyone can access to it. To change password open again terminal and run command “passwd”, then it going to ask you old password, enter “toor”and click enter, and enter new password (does not metter what it will be) and remem",,,,,GUNCELLIK_KONTROL,ORTA,root/toor eski Kali imajına özgü olabilir; genel güncel Kali varsayılanı olarak kullanılamaz ve parola bilgisini yanlış bağlama taşıyabilir.,,1.00,"“Bridged Adapter” this means that program will use your built-in wireless adapter. Now you are ready to start virtual machine. Click “Start” and wait before username promt appears. the default username is “root”, and default password is “toor”, but for security we going to change it later. The screen should look like this: On the left side should be program called “terminal”, click on it and you will see that black screen appears with red promt “root@kali#”. You may have question like “what does root means?”, well root is an access type, to",GUNCELLIK_KONTROL,ORTA,root/toor eski Kali imajına özgü olabilir; genel güncel Kali varsayılanı olarak kullanılamaz ve parola bilgisini yanlış bağlama taşıyabilir.,,1.00,"“Bridged Adapter” this means that program will use your built-in wireless adapter. Now you are ready to start virtual machine. Click “Start” and wait before username promt appears. the default username is “root”, and default password is “toor”, but for security we going to change it later. The screen should look like this: On the left side should be program called “terminal”, click on it and you will see that black screen appears with red promt “root@kali#”. You may have question like “what does root means?”, well root is an access type, to"
162,batch_new500_0219,val,System Security,Beyond Model Scaling_ Rethinking Sequence Construction for T.txt,What is the minimum input representation that achieves the highest Macro-F1 score according to the study?,The per-flow representation achieves the highest Macro-F1 score of 0.761 according to the study.,"Instead, it arises from exposing the transformer to behaviorally coherent input sequences. This result identifies temporalization, rather than the learning architecture itself, as the dominant bottleneck in flow-based intrusion detection. Representation Cannot Recover Lost Behavioral Context. To verify that the observed gains are not specific to a particular traffic encoding, we fix the temporalization strategy and transformer architecture while varying only the input representation. Although the per-flow representation achieves the highest Macro-F1 (0.761), followed by fieldtoken (0.580) and serialized-text (0.562), these differences are modest compared with the 2.2× improvement achieved by session-coherent temporalization (Fig. 2). This demonstrates that traffic representation influences how behavioral information is encoded, whereas temporalization determines whether that information is available to the model. Consequently, once behavioral continuity is lost during sequence construction, no input representation alone can recover it. should be treated as a first-class systems design decision rather than a fixed preprocessing step. Once coherent behavioral context is preserved, compact transformer models can accurately model multi-stage attacks without substantially increasing model capacity. We next ask whether preserving behavioral context still requires larger transformers. B. RQ2: Behavioral Context over Model Scale Finding. Once behavioral context is preserved through session-coherent temporalization, increasing transformer capacity yields rapidly diminishing returns. Moderate-capacity models achieve detection performance comparable to that of substantially larger architectures while sustaining significantly higher inference throughput. Fig. 3 evaluates transformer capacity under identical session-coherent temporalization across a grid of embedding dimensions, transformer depths, and attention heads. Because temporalization remains fixed, the experiment isolat",,,,,YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,Ağ akışı temsili ile sınıflandırma performansı.,Network Security,0.71,"only the input representation. Although the per-flow representation achieves the highest Macro-F1 (0.761), followed by fieldtoken (0.580) and serialized-text (0.562), these differences are modest compared with the 2.2× improvement achieved by session-coherent temporalization (Fig. 2). This demonstrates that traffic representation influences how behavioral information is encoded, whereas temporalization determines whether that information is available to the model. Consequently, once behavioral continuity is lost during sequence construction, no",YANLIS_KONU,ORTA,Ağ akışı temsili ile sınıflandırma performansı.,Network Security,0.71,"only the input representation. Although the per-flow representation achieves the highest Macro-F1 (0.761), followed by fieldtoken (0.580) and serialized-text (0.562), these differences are modest compared with the 2.2× improvement achieved by session-coherent temporalization (Fig. 2). This demonstrates that traffic representation influences how behavioral information is encoded, whereas temporalization determines whether that information is available to the model. Consequently, once behavioral continuity is lost during sequence construction, no"
163,draft_0103,val,System Security,PIMROP_ A Feasibility Study of Return-Oriented Programming o.txt,What is the reason for the stack canary failing in the defense-gap analysis?,"The stack canary fails due to an architectural issue where the DPU stack frame grows toward higher addresses. This causes a callee to save its return pair {r22, r23} above its local buffer, while the compiler places the canary below it. Consequently, a linear overflow DMA (Direct Memory Access) moves upward from the buffer into the saved return pair, bypassing the canary entirely.","Defense-Gap Analysis We probed each standard mitigation on the DPU side. ASLR is absent because code lives at a fixed IRAM base of 0x80000000 and the WRAM stack is deterministic, so the exploit reproduced 10 of 10 runs from a single hard-coded payload and every gadget and sink address is known offline. The DPU also lacks any CFI or pointer-authentication. The net result is that none of the host-side protections in Table I has a working counterpart on the DPU, which is exactly why the overflow discussed in Section VII-C is exploitable with a single static payload. TABLE II: Mitigation experiment (N=10 per build). Leak = secret in output_buf; caught = canary trip; clean = Baseline (no mitigation) Stack canary (runtime supplied) Stack canaries fail in two separate ways. First they are unavailable out of the box: the compiler front end accepts -fstack-protector-all and emits canary checks, but linking fails on undefined __stack_chk_guard and __stack_chk_fail, so a stack-protected kernel cannot be built at all. We removed this obstacle with a minimal runtime that defines a guard word and a __stack_chk_fail handler that halts. A protected kernel then links. Even so, the canary does not stop the attack: refiring the same exploit against the hardened kernel still leaks the secret 10 of 10 while the canary trips 0 of 10 (Table II). The reason is architectural. The DPU stack frame grows toward higher addresses, so a callee saves its return pair {r22,r23} above its local buffer whereas the compiler places the canary below it. A linear overflow DMAs upward from the buffer into the saved return and never touches build: we swept 144 configurations of the vulnerable kernel (six optimization levels, six buffer sizes from 32 to 1024 bytes, with and without frame-pointer omission, at 1 or 4 tasklets), and every build placed the canary slot at the lowest offset of the frame. We therefore treat the misplacement as a property of the toolchain port, requiring a backend fix rather than pe",,,,,ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.68,"does not stop the attack: refiring the same exploit against the hardened kernel still leaks the secret 10 of 10 while the canary trips 0 of 10 (Table II). The reason is architectural. The DPU stack frame grows toward higher addresses, so a callee saves its return pair {r22,r23} above its local buffer whereas the compiler places the canary below it. A linear overflow DMAs upward from the buffer into the saved return and never touches build: we swept 144 configurations of the vulnerable kernel (six optimization levels, six buffer sizes from 32",ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.68,"does not stop the attack: refiring the same exploit against the hardened kernel still leaks the secret 10 of 10 while the canary trips 0 of 10 (Table II). The reason is architectural. The DPU stack frame grows toward higher addresses, so a callee saves its return pair {r22,r23} above its local buffer whereas the compiler places the canary below it. A linear overflow DMAs upward from the buffer into the saved return and never touches build: we swept 144 configurations of the vulnerable kernel (six optimization levels, six buffer sizes from 32"
164,draft_0034,test,System Security,ExploreRepair_ Evidence-Specialized Agents for Vulnerability.txt,What specific protection is missing in the affected function that handles simple requests through a shortcut?,The specific protection missing in the affected function that handles simple requests through a shortcut is the safety check for names supplied to a database query.,"The trajectory records the input, the observed failure, and the response to the repair. Passing the generated PoV supports the agent’s diagnosis, but does not guarantee that its patch passes the hidden benchmark PoV. During aggregation, the agents must therefore check these execution observations against the repository and the other agents’ findings. # fields contains the names requested by the user. def set_values(self, fields): # Simple request: take the shortcut. if not self.extra and not self.annotations: # Copy the names without checking safety. field_names = list(fields) # More complex request: process each name. self.default_cols = False # f is one requested name. # No safety check here either. Listing 1: Original Django code: both paths lack the safety check. Dots stand for code omitted from the Qualitative Aggregation Analysis We examine two cases in which aggregation produces a new fix or loses a correct one. Both cases Producing a Fix from Unsuccessful CVE-2024-42005 affects how Django handles names supplied to a database query. These names must be checked for dangerous characters; otherwise, an attacker can use a crafted name to change the meaning of the database command, causing SQL injection. The affected function handles simple requests through a shortcut and more complex requests through a separate path (Listing 1). The missing protection is the same in both: the names are used without the required safety check. Each exploration agent finds part of the problem, as shown in Listing 2. The Code Knowledge Graph agent checks names on the complex path, but misses the shortcut. The Intent agent adds a check in another function that creates query names. The PoV agent adds # to the list of forbidden characters, but does not make either path perform the check. All three repairs fail the benchmark PoV test because the attack takes the unchecked shortThe Lesson Aggregator uses these findings to inspect the function again and notices that the shortcut still has ",,,,,ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.93,"a Fix from Unsuccessful CVE-2024-42005 affects how Django handles names supplied to a database query. These names must be checked for dangerous characters; otherwise, an attacker can use a crafted name to change the meaning of the database command, causing SQL injection. The affected function handles simple requests through a shortcut and more complex requests through a separate path (Listing 1). The missing protection is the same in both: the names are used without the required safety check. Each exploration agent finds part of the problem, as",ILK_TARAMADA_BELIRGIN_HATA_YOK,DUSUK,"Soru-cevapta ilk taramada belirgin çelişki yakalanmadı. Bu doğruluk, uzman onayı veya güncellik doğrulaması DEĞİLDİR.",,0.93,"a Fix from Unsuccessful CVE-2024-42005 affects how Django handles names supplied to a database query. These names must be checked for dangerous characters; otherwise, an attacker can use a crafted name to change the meaning of the database command, causing SQL injection. The affected function handles simple requests through a shortcut and more complex requests through a separate path (Listing 1). The missing protection is the same in both: the names are used without the required safety check. Each exploration agent finds part of the problem, as"
165,batch1000_0726,test,System Security,Extending Layered Attestation into ARM Application Run-Times.txt,What are the primary functions of a Root of Trust for Measurement (RTM)?,"RTM primarily enables secure boot, cryptographic key management, and platform remote integrity verification. It focuses on system integrity by securely measuring software, including load-time code integrity and run-time integrity, such as control and data flow.","In modern systems, RoTs enable functions such as secure boot, cryptographic key management, and platform remote integrity verification (a.k.a., remote attestation). RoTs are generally categorized as RoTs for measurement and A Root of Trust for Measurement (RTM) focuses on system integrity by securely measuring software (either statically, i.e., at load-time or run-time/execution properties). Examples of measured properties include load-time code integrity and run-time integrity (e.g., control and data flow). A Root of Trust for Storage (RTS) provides secure protection for sensitive cryptographic material and other security-critical data. Unlike an RTM, which focuses on integrity measurement, the RTS ensures the confidentiality and controlled usage of secrets such as encryption keys, certificates, authentication credentials, and attestation keys. In many architectures, cryptographic operations involving protected keys are performed entirely within the RTS boundary, preventing key material from ever being exposed in plaintext to untrusted software. ARA establishes a run-time RoT within a user-space process. Section 7 presents two case studies demonstrating how ARA can be instantiated as RTM and RTS for user-space Layered Attestation and Application Integrity Modern mobile platforms (such as iOS and Android) provide hardware-backed RTMs for attestation services that allow application servers to verify the integrity of both application code and aspects of the underlying execution environment 1Some of the literature distinguishes a third category, namely RoT for Reporting (RTR), used when the RTM result is to be signed to generate an externally verifiable report that can be checked by a remote verifier, e.g., in remote attestation protocols. In this paper, we deliberately couple RTR as a sub-function of RTM. sions for domains based on their IDs at or near load-time. Two prominent examples are Apple’s App Attest [2] and Google’s Play Integrity API [24]. These systems aim ",,,,,DUZELT,YUKSEK,Yanıt Root of Trust ailesinin secure boot/anahtar yönetimini RTM özel işlevi gibi anlatıyor; kaynak RTM için yalnızca ölçüm/bütünlük odağı belirtiyor.,,0.91,"In modern systems, RoTs enable functions such as secure boot, cryptographic key management, and platform remote integrity verification (a.k.a., remote attestation). RoTs are generally categorized as RoTs for measurement and A Root of Trust for Measurement (RTM) focuses on system integrity by securely measuring software (either statically, i.e., at load-time or run-time/execution properties). Examples of measured properties include load-time code integrity and run-time integrity (e.g., control and data flow). A Root of Trust for Storage (RTS) pr",DUZELT,YUKSEK,Yanıt Root of Trust ailesinin secure boot/anahtar yönetimini RTM özel işlevi gibi anlatıyor; kaynak RTM için yalnızca ölçüm/bütünlük odağı belirtiyor.,,0.91,"In modern systems, RoTs enable functions such as secure boot, cryptographic key management, and platform remote integrity verification (a.k.a., remote attestation). RoTs are generally categorized as RoTs for measurement and A Root of Trust for Measurement (RTM) focuses on system integrity by securely measuring software (either statically, i.e., at load-time or run-time/execution properties). Examples of measured properties include load-time code integrity and run-time integrity (e.g., control and data flow). A Root of Trust for Storage (RTS) pr"
166,batch1000_0472,train,Web Security,BTK Akademi_Siber Güvenliğe Giriş_Atıl Samancıoğlu.txt,What are the three basic protocols used for securing wireless networks?,"WEP, WPA, and WPA2 (points/wpa3-dep-guide-og.html) are the three basic protocols used for securing wireless networks.","Kablosuz ağ güvenliği, ağın gizliliğini, bütünlüğünü ve erişilebilirliğini korumayı amaçlar. Kablosuz ağ güvenliği, kablosuz (Wi-Fi) ağların yetkisiz erişime karşı korunması ve güvende tutulması anlamına gelir. Bu koruma yöntemleri ağ trafiğinin şifrelenmesi ve yetkisiz erişimlere karşı savunma sağlar. Kablosuz ağ güvenliği için kullanılan temel protokoller şunlardır: WEP, WPA ve points/wpa3-dep-guide-og.html OWASP (Open Web Application Security • OWASP, ""Open Web Application Security Project"" kelimelerinin baş harflerinden oluşan bir kısaltmadır ve açık kaynaklı bir topluluk tarafından yönetilen bir projeyi ifade • OWASP, yazılım ve web uygulamalarının güvenliğini artırmayı amaçlayan bir dizi kaynak ve rehber sunar. OWASP, web uygulama güvenliği alanında dünya genelinde tanınan bir otoritedir. • OWASP, geliştiricilere, güvenlik profesyonellerine ve organizasyonlara aşağıdaki konularda yardımcı olur: Güvenli Uygulama Geliştirme Siber Tehditlere Karşı Koruma Eğitim ve Bilinçlendirme OWASP kaynakları, yazılım geliştiricileri, siber güvenlik profesyonelleri, bilgi güvenliği uzmanları ve organizasyonlar tarafından kullanılır. saldırılardan kaynaklanan veri sızıntıları ve maddi kayıpları önlemelerine yardımcı olabilir. OWASP, yazılım güvenliği için bir standart oluşturur ve bu nedenle büyük bir öneme • Güvenlik amaçlı kod, yazılım geliştirme sürecinde güvenlik programlama kodlarını ifade eder. Bu kodlar, yazılımın siber saldırılara ve güvenlik ihlallerine karşı daha dayanıklı olmasını noktalarını tespit eder ve düzeltilmesine yardımcı olur. Statik Kod Analizi: Bu, yazılımın kaynak kodunun incelemesiyle gerçekleştirilen bir güvenlik Otomatik analiz araçları kullanılarak kod üzerinde potans